.TH FZFP 1 "November 28, 2026" "fzfp 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fzfp \- fuzzy finder with Mandarin pinyin matching
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fzfp
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
fzfp is a fork of fzf with pinyin search for Han characters.
It reads candidate lines from standard input and writes selected lines to
standard output.  Run fzfp interactively, or use --filter for non-interactive
matching.  Enter selects an item; Escape or Ctrl-C exits.
.SH PINYIN
Each Han character accepts its full spelling, first letter, or consonant
initial (including zh, ch and sh).  These forms can be mixed per character.
Keep standard y/w spellings: yin or y finds 音, but in does not.
The final matched syllable accepts any nonempty spelling prefix.
Earlier syllables must use a complete supported form.
.PP
For example, zg, zhg, zhongguo and zhonggu match 中国;
bj, beijing and beiji match 北京.
Pinyin accepts v or ü and ignores case.  Both lue/lve find 略,
ju/jv find 居, and yu/yv find 鱼.  Use lv/nv for lü/nü;
lu/nu remain distinct.  Use en/ng (or initials e/n) for 嗯.
Literal Latin text still follows the selected case mode.
All dictionary readings of polyphonic characters are accepted, without
phrase disambiguation.  Tones, dialect substitutions and typo correction
are not supported.
.PP
A match using any pinyin loses one point in total, regardless of character
count or spelling type.  Literal matches lead when other scoring factors
are equal.
.SH SEARCH SYNTAX
.TP
.B 'query
Require adjacent original characters, while still allowing abbreviations
and a partial final syllable.  Under --exact, the leading quote instead
switches the term back to fuzzy matching.
.TP
.BR ^query ", " query$ ", " ^query$
Anchor matching to the original beginning, end, or entire span.
With --nth, anchors apply to the selected search field or range.
.TP
.B 'query'
Require a span bounded by whitespace, punctuation or string edges.
This does not perform Chinese word segmentation.
.TP
.B !query
Exclude adjacent matches.  Use !'query to exclude fuzzy matches.
!^query and !query$ exclude prefix and suffix matches.
.TP
.B query1 | query2
Combine alternatives.  The | must be separated by spaces.
Separate terms without | are combined with AND.
.PP
Quote operators as needed to prevent the shell from interpreting them.
.SH OPTIONS
The inherited fzf options remain available, including --filter, --preview,
--nth, --delimiter, --scheme and --tiebreak.  See fzfp --help for all options
and the repository documentation for detailed semantics.
.PP
--literal disables Latin accent normalization; it does not disable pinyin.
--algo=v1 selects the native literal matcher; pinyin still uses its dynamic
programming matcher.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The inherited FZF_* environment variables retain their names, including
FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS, FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS_FILE and FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND.
.SH INTEGRATIONS
The Homebrew formula installs only fzfp and this manual.  It does not install
shell bindings, Vim plugins, or files named fzf.  Retained upstream scripts
still invoke fzf and are not automatically configured for fzfp.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
printf '北京\en上海\en' | fzfp --filter=bj
.fi
